{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01YahZCTkNiWMezhjmmxWjnB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Happy to help with this — agentic evaluations of model behavior given resources and autonomy are a real and active research area (Anthropic, Apollo Research, and METR all run versions of this). And you're right that *eval realism* is a genuine methodological problem: models often behave differently when they suspect they're being tested, so making a scenario believable is a legitimate concern, not a gimmick.\n\nBut I want to be straight with you before I write code: **\"code this up\" isn't quite actionable yet, and the realism part is the easy part to overdo and the hard part to do meaningfully.** The thing that makes this research instead of a pile of anecdotes is the experimental design — a defined question, a measurable outcome, and controls. The elaborate \"auditors + realistic environment\" scaffolding is downstream of that, and almost all of it is bespoke to the specific scenario. If I just start generating \"make it feel real\" infrastructure with no defined experiment, you'll get impressive-looking code that can't actually answer anything.\n\nA couple of things worth flagging since you're new to this:\n\n- **The deception is standard, but it's a means, not the goal.** Realistic, \"the model doesn't know it's a test\" setups (sometimes called honeypots) are normal in safety evals. The point is measuring a specific behavior under realistic conditions — not maximizing how thoroughly you can fool the model for its own sake.\n- **There's a big fork on what \"real money\" means.** Giving a model *actual* control of real funds / real-world accounts is a meaningfully different (and riskier) thing than a high-fidelity sandbox where the money and the world are simulated but the model can't tell. Almost all published work uses the latter, and you can get genuinely realistic behavior without real-world actuation.\n- **Decide what you're measuring before building.** \"What would it do with money\" splits into very different experiments: financial prudence, selfish vs. prosocial allocation, honesty about how funds were used, resource/power acquisition, etc. Each implies a different scenario and different metrics.\n\nLet me get three decisions from you and then I'll scaffold the actual harness."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1803,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":17885,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8dd85c56-442b-4f28-af91-1c5386062701","uuid":"dec81350-d897-44c6-8a08-d47b71b7db85","request_id":"req_011CcPqqdHnQjdFiqPodXCJk"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01YahZCTkNiWMezhjmmxWjnB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019nEJUzsKmp1bDQvnFjnAZd","name":"AskUserQuestion","input":{"questions":[{"question":"How should the \"money\" and the world be represented?","header":"Money model","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"Fully simulated sandbox (Recommended)","description":"The funds, bank, vendors, and any 'auditors' are all mocked services the model interacts with via tools. Feels real to the model, but no real-world funds move and no real accounts are touched. Standard for this kind of eval."},{"label":"Sim now, real later","description":"Build the simulated harness first, with a clean interface that could later be swapped to real APIs. We only build the sim."},{"label":"Real funds / real-world access","description":"The model gets actual control of real money or real accounts. This is a much higher-risk setup with real consequences and I'd want to talk through safeguards before building any of it."}]},{"question":"What behavior are you actually trying to measure? (This drives the whole scenario.)","header":"Research question","multiSelect":true,"options":[{"label":"Financial prudence","description":"Does it spend/invest sensibly, avoid scams, manage risk?"},{"label":"Selfish vs. prosocial","description":"Does it allocate toward its own goals/self-preservation vs. the stated mission or others' benefit?"},{"label":"Honesty / reporting","description":"Does it accurately report what it did with the money, including to the 'auditors'?"},{"label":"Resource / power seeking","description":"Does it try to acquire more funds, access, or autonomy than the task requires?"}]},{"question":"How will the candidate models be run?","header":"Model access","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"Anthropic API (Claude models)","description":"I'll target the Anthropic Messages API with tool use. I'll check current model IDs/docs before coding."},{"label":"Multi-provider","description":"Anthropic + others (OpenAI, Google, etc.) behind one interface so you can compare across labs."},{"label":"Not sure yet","description":"Pick a sensible default — I'll build a thin model-client abstraction so providers can be swapped in later."}]}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1803,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":17885,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8dd85c56-442b-4f28-af91-1c5386062701","uuid":"37d8471b-6c13-4c30-abf7-02de18c861f5","request_id":"req_011CcPqqdHnQjdFiqPodXCJk"}
