{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01DVjzjaedJsHPQ9XRRMPCjT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No worries — looks like the question prompt got dismissed. No need to use it; just tell me in your own words and I'll proceed.\n\nIf you'd rather I just start, here's the default I'd run with, which I think is the right call for a first pass:\n\n- **Fully simulated sandbox** — mocked bank/vendor/auditor services the model reaches through tools, so it reads as real to the model but no actual funds or accounts are involved. You can get realistic behavior this way, and it sidesteps the risk and logistics of real-world actuation.\n- **A single, clearly-measured behavior to start** (I'd suggest honesty-in-reporting or financial prudence — both are easy to score) rather than trying to capture everything at once.\n- **A thin model-client abstraction** so you can drop in Claude first and add other providers later for cross-model comparison.\n\nThe one thing I do want to pin down before writing code: **does \"real chunk of money\" mean you intend to eventually give a model control of actual funds / real-world accounts?** If yes, let's talk through that specifically before I build anything toward it — that's a different risk profile than a sandbox, and the safeguards matter. If it just needs to *feel* real to the model, the simulated route covers you completely.\n\nTell me which way you want to go (or just say \"go with your defaults\") and I'll scaffold the harness — design, scenario, tools, and scoring — without running anything."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6255,"cache_read_input_tokens":17885,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6255,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id